1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,800
The work was already done.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,800
Delivered, stamped, invoiced.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,800
And the money arrived in sixty days.

4
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:27,600
We decided to become parents anyway.

5
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:45,800
Every night I typed by hand
what was already inside an XML file.

6
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:51,800
And even so, nobody was going to
take our books on faith.

7
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:59,900
We were about to lose
the very thing we wanted to protect.

8
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:05,800
So we stopped doing it alone.

9
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:11,800
Intake. Validation. Audit. Ledger.

10
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:16,800
And if an invoice was already
assigned, it rejects it.

11
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:23,800
It works at night.
With nobody touching it.

12
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:31,800
Every day it publishes the fingerprint
of the whole day, outside our own servers.

13
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:36,800
[ Base Sepolia — the anchoring transaction,
on a public explorer that is not ours ]

14
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:41,800
We sleep.

15
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:45,800
Someone changed a number.

16
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:51,800
The system named the exact row.

17
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:57,800
And it refused to publish.
Signing a broken chain is worse than not signing.

18
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:04,800
Freedom was never about producing more.

19
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:16,800
It was about being there.

20
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:31,500
CØRD. The agent works at night.
The proof is public.
